{{also|Kîo|ki'o|kiò}}
==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
From {{af|eo|ki-|pos1=interrogative and relative [[:Category:Esperanto correlatives|correlative]] prefix|-o|pos2=correlative suffix of objects|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{eo-IPA|a=Eo-kio.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|eo|pronoun|accusative singular|kion}}

# [[what]] (the interrogative and relative correlative of objects)
# [[which]]
#: {{ux|eo|Mi daŭrigis mian laboron, ĝis kiam iu knabo aŭ virino diris "bagus, bagus", '''kio''' signifas "tre bela".|I continued my work, until some boy or woman said "bagus, bagus", which means "very pretty".}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|eo|kio ajn|t=[[whatever]]}}

===Usage notes===
* Like other correlatives of objects, and unlike {{cog|en|what}}, {{m|eo||kio}} always functions as a pronoun, never an adjective.
* The plural forms {{m|eo|kioj}} and {{m|eo|kiojn}} are nonstandard and rare.

